  "answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-phase initiative focused on data analytics, cloud storage optimization, and AI-driven data visualization. Key details include:\n\n- **Leadership & Timeline**: Led by Sarah Tan (Analytics) and Marcus Cole, with kick-offs scheduled for June 15th, July 15th, and a launch date of December 12, 2024. The project spans Q3 2023 through 2024.\n- **Budget**: Initial phase budget was $500,000, later adjusted to $550,000 to cover real-time analytics integration. An additional $15,000 was approved for training programs.\n- **Objectives**: Revolutionize data analytics, optimize cloud storage for security/accessibility, and enhance data visualization tools using AI.\n- **Milestones & Updates**: A secure file sharing prototype was successfully tested ahead of schedule. Security protocols (MFA, encryption) are being updated for January. Feedback is being sought by November.\n- **Collaboration**: R&D is submitting ideas by July 20th, and partnerships with TechInnovate for AI technology are being explored."
